{"tool_name":"informed-proteomics","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"informed-proteomics","home":"https://github.com/PNNL-Comp-Mass-Spec/Informed-Proteomics","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"A suite for top-down proteomics analysis that consists of an LC-MS feature-finding algorithm, a database search algorithm, and an interactive results viewer.","addition_date":"2018-06-04T14:29:56Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T13:47:49.654721Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"collections":["Proteomics"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:informed-proteomics","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"matthew.monroe@pnnl.gov","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/PNNL-Comp-Mass-Spec/Informed-Proteomics/wiki"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Spectrum","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_3483"},"format":[{"term":"mzML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3244"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Mass spectrum visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3694"},{"term":"Protein identification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3767"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2048"},"format":[{"term":"Workflow format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2032"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"Informed-Proteomics","operating_system":["Windows"],"owner":"ELIXIR-EE","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/nmeth.4388","metadata":{"abstract":"Top-down proteomics, the analysis of intact proteins in their endogenous form, preserves valuable information about post-translation modifications, isoforms and proteolytic processing. The quality of top-down liquid chromatography-tandem MS (LC-MS/MS) data sets is rapidly increasing on account of advances in instrumentation and sample-processing protocols. However, top-down mass spectra are substantially more complex than conventional bottom-up data. New algorithms and software tools for confident proteoform identification and quantification are needed. Here we present Informed-Proteomics, an open-source software suite for top-down proteomics analysis that consists of an LC-MS feature-finding algorithm, a database search algorithm, and an interactive results viewer. We compare our tool with several other popular tools using human-in-mouse xenograft luminal and basal breast tumor samples that are known to have significant differences in protein abundance based on bottom-up analysis.","authors":[{"name":"Fujimoto G.M."},{"name":"Gibbons B.C."},{"name":"Kim S."},{"name":"Liu T."},{"name":"Mendoza J."},{"name":"Moore R.J."},{"name":"Park J."},{"name":"Pasa-Tolic L."},{"name":"Payne S.H."},{"name":"Petyuk V.A."},{"name":"Piehowski P.D."},{"name":"Shaw J.B."},{"name":"Shen Y."},{"name":"Shukla A.K."},{"name":"Smith R.D."},{"name":"Tolic N."},{"name":"Wilkins C."},{"name":"Zhou M."}],"citationCount":120,"date":"2017-08-31T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"Informed-Proteomics: Open-source software package for top-down proteomics"},"pmcid":"PMC5578875","pmid":"28783154"}],"topic":[{"term":"Molecular biology","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3047"},{"term":"Proteins","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0078"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"Informed-Proteomics","home":"https://bio.tools/informed-proteomics","license":"Apache-2.0","summary":"A suite for top-down proteomics analysis that consists of an LC-MS feature-finding algorithm, a database search algorithm, and an interactive results viewer.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:informed-proteomics/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"dist